    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0951" n="925" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v10/pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">888.2553/2–1854: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 425<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the
                        Embassy in Iran</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-02-18T18:47:00-05:00">February 18, 1954—6:47
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1745. Limit distribution. Following is report Secretary’s conversation with Eden
                    Feb 17 Berlin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Iran. I said I did not think Anglo-Iranian could hold 50 per cent
                            position. We were not trying to get larger US position, but only trying
                            to meet political realities in Iran. Eden said that he had thought 50
                            per cent probably unobtainable, but hoped to get as close to this as
                            possible with position for Dutch Shell. I emphasized US companies were
                            not themselves seeking large participation, but only going along at
                            Government request and that our judgment would be entirely a political
                            judgment based on estimate Iran situation.</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
